    "Picture/map estimates: occupied podium34.4m wide and about40m deep, local floor3.4m above anchor datum and broad18-step approach. Three white Corinthian columns15.2m above floor plus roughly1.2m entablature; four broken front shafts retain distinct heights4.6/2.6/2.9/2.4m. High firewall top29m above datum, lower right return15.5m; approximate Pantani opening4.6m wide,5m spring and7.3m crown. Hidden cella/apse allocation, wall ruin inventory, masonry holes/repairs and absolute archaeological levels remain approximate.",
